K	DiagTrack	svc	19045	Connected User Experiences and Telemetry	Collects and sends Windows diagnostic and usage data to Microsoft.	Diagnostic data upload stops. Feedback Hub and some troubleshooters report less; Windows keeps working.	Disable, restart, use the PC as usual for a few days; check that Windows Update still runs.	4			telemetry upload, not needed for anything on the PC itself			0	0	published	Microsoft's IoT Enterprise services page (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/iot/iot-enterprise/optimize/services) describes this service (Windows 10/11 IoT Enterprise services page). What breaks is Hadron's reasoning unless a source is named.	published	Microsoft's IoT Enterprise services page (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/iot/iot-enterprise/optimize/services) rates it "OK to disable" (Windows 10/11 IoT Enterprise) and Microsoft's VDI optimization tool (Windows 10 20H2+ virtual desktops) (https://github.com/The-Virtual-Desktop-Team/Virtual-Desktop-Optimization-Tool/blob/main/2009/ConfigurationFiles/Services.json) disables it; Microsoft's Windows Server 2016 service guidance (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/security/windows-services/security-guidelines-for-disabling-system-services-in-windows-server) rates it "No guidance" (Windows Server 2016), which Hadron reads as keep the default. Microsoft's Windows 10 2004 VDI guide (archived) (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/remote/remote-desktop-services/rds-vdi-recommendations-2004) lists it as a candidate on disconnected networks.						
